      "explanationAfterStep": "Losing the last proton gives the 1,4-dihydropyridine: two enamines conjugated with two esters, which makes it stable enough to isolate. It is not yet aromatic: an oxidant (for example HNO₃) removes two more hydrogens to give the pyridine."
    }
